item+ function src/http.rs :: percent_decode :: pub fn percent_decode(s: &str) -> String { :: Percent-decode a URL path segment string. `+` is left alone (it is a literal plus in a path, not a space). Invalid sequences pass through unchanged; the caller's path rules reject anything odd. :: doc comment :: 371 :: 1
item+ function src/http.rs :: xml_escape :: pub fn xml_escape(s: &str) -> String { :: XML-escape text for the RSS feed (same five characters as HTML, without the apostrophe form XML parsers also accept). Control characters XML 1.0 forbids outright — everything below U+0020 except tab, line feed, and carriage return — are replaced with U+FFFD: left raw, a single one (a stray bell or vertical tab in a markdown source, say) makes the whole feed not well-formed, and every subscriber's parser refuses it — the same silent death as one unescaped `&`, by another character. :: doc comment :: 350 :: 1
